# ── Optional server defaults ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything here is optional. Users can paste their own credentials into
# /settings (bring-your-own-key); values entered there take precedence for that
# request and are never written to disk. Use this file when you want a shared
# default for local development or a self-hosted deployment.

# ── GitHub ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public read-only access is enough. A token raises you to 5,000 req/hr, which is
# the difference between a working demo and a 403.
# Create one at https://github.com/settings/tokens (classic, no scopes needed for
# public data) or a fine-grained token with read-only access to public repos.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ── Model provider ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Google AI Studio exposes an OpenAI-compatible endpoint, so the same adapter
# works for AI Studio, OpenRouter, Ollama, or anything else that speaks the
# OpenAI chat-completions protocol.
# Get a key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
LLM_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/
LLM_API_KEY=
# Confirm the exact model id in AI Studio before relying on it.
LLM_MODEL=gemma-4-31b-it

# ── Behaviour ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1 = serve only from cache (use this on stage). 0 = allow live network calls.
COMPASS_OFFLINE=0
COMPASS_CACHE_DIR=.cache
